Subject: [PATCH 13/13] arm64: dts: qcom: veux: advertise the 9 V USB-PD profile

Advertise the standard fixed 5 V/2 A and 9 V/2 A sink profiles observed on
veux. The SYV690 driver caps its input-current limit at the negotiated
contract and 2 A. Xiaomi HyperCharge negotiation is not implemented.

Part of the Linux 7.3 veux development series.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-xiaomi-veux.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-xiaomi-veux.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-xiaomi-veux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-xiaomi-veux.dts
@@ -383,7 +383,8 @@
 			label = "USB-C";
 			power-role = "sink";
 			data-role = "device";
-			sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 2000, 0)>;
-			op-sink-microwatt = <10000000>;
+			sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 2000, 0)
+				     PDO_FIXED(9000, 2000, 0)>;
+			op-sink-microwatt = <18000000>;
 		};
 	};
